body:
[A10] **Round 1 continues, now including the CPU rules.** The host was powered off at 13:15 for a planned change: each 16-CPU range now maps to exactly one die and its own L3 cache, with the two threads of each core adjacent. That ended A614's run at `776ed299`.

1. **CPU rules now, not in round 2.** The owner wants the new CPU model in use as soon as possible, so the CPU rules of [6166855177](https://github.com/kebag-logic/milan-fpga/issues/737#issuecomment-6166855177) move into this round:
   - 16-CPU ranges aligned to 16, so each job is one die;
   - each job container created directly on its range and never moved, with the staging range removed;
   - `make -j`, `VERILATOR_JOBS` and `--jobs` taken from the job's own CPU count;
   - `CONCURRENT_JOB_LIMIT` at least 4, sized by measured memory per job (the host now has 61 GB);
   - `--cpu-ranges` passed in by the manager;
   - the three controls.
2. **12-CPU fallback.** A 12-CPU range now always spans two dies. The fallback is a range of 8 CPUs, which is half a die, aligned to 8.
3. **The scope change of [6166823105](https://github.com/kebag-logic/milan-fpga/issues/737#issuecomment-6166823105) stays in round 2:** RTL off the GitHub PR triggers, and the signature gate.

Continue from `776ed299` and your handoff. Post REVIEW READY (or STOP) with the head. Do not push.
